\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {13.2}Code organisation}{97}{section.13.2}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces Organisation of PRoNTo's functions. From the developer's perspective the code is organised in functions and sub functions that deal with the user interface experience (such as GUI and batch functions), the core functions that implement the machine learning approaches (including extracting and preparing the features, specification and estimation of a model, cross-validation routines, etc.) and the actual machine learning algorithms (also known as machines).}}{98}{figure.13.1}}
\newlabel{Fig1.1}{{13.1}{98}{Organisation of PRoNTo's functions. From the developer's perspective the code is organised in functions and sub functions that deal with the user interface experience (such as GUI and batch functions), the core functions that implement the machine learning approaches (including extracting and preparing the features, specification and estimation of a model, cross-validation routines, etc.) and the actual machine learning algorithms (also known as machines)}{figure.13.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {13.2.1}User interface}{98}{subsection.13.2.1}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {13.2.2}Machine learning}{98}{subsection.13.2.2}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {13.2.3}Machines}{98}{subsection.13.2.3}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.2}{\ignorespaces Code organisation for integrating a new machine with PRoNTo. `prt$\_$machine.m' works has a wrapper that translates PRoNTo's inputs into the machine format inputs and performs extensive error checks on these variables. The machines (such as `prt$\_$machine$\_$svm$\_$bin.m') perform the classifier/regression algorithms and have inputs and outputs that are not dependent on PRoNTo's internal structures.}}{99}{figure.13.2}}
\newlabel{Fig1.2}{{13.2}{99}{Code organisation for integrating a new machine with PRoNTo. `prt$\_$machine.m' works has a wrapper that translates PRoNTo's inputs into the machine format inputs and performs extensive error checks on these variables. The machines (such as `prt$\_$machine$\_$svm$\_$bin.m') perform the classifier/regression algorithms and have inputs and outputs that are not dependent on PRoNTo's internal structures}{figure.13.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.3}{\ignorespaces `prt$\_$machine$\_$.m' function help. Example of a PRoNTo machine for 2-class SVM classification.}}{100}{figure.13.3}}
\newlabel{Fig1.3}{{13.3}{100}{`prt$\_$machine$\_$.m' function help. Example of a PRoNTo machine for 2-class SVM classification}{figure.13.3}{}}
